From: rhodep port <none@example.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 01:10:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: ipa: do not add the memory offset to a size

init_modem_driver_req() tells the modem where its hardware statistics regions
are and how big they are:

	req.hw_stats_quota_base_addr = ipa->mem_offset + mem->offset;
	req.hw_stats_quota_size = ipa->mem_offset + mem->size;

The base address is right. The size is not. `ipa->mem_offset` is where IPA's
local memory starts, read from SHARED_MEM_SIZE, and it belongs in an address,
not in a length. The same mistake is repeated for the drop statistics region.

Downstream sends the plain size for both:

	req.hw_stats_quota_size = IPA_MEM_PART(stats_quota_q6_size);
	req.hw_drop_stats_table_size = IPA_MEM_PART(stats_drop_size);

If mem_offset is zero on a given SoC this never mattered, which is presumably
why it has survived. Where it is not zero, the modem is told a region is that
many bytes longer than it is, and the quota region here is 0x30 bytes with the
AP's own quota region immediately after it at 0x1d30.

Send the size.
---
--- a/drivers/net/ipa/ipa_qmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ipa/ipa_qmi.c
@@ -380,7 +380,7 @@
 			req.hw_stats_quota_base_addr =
 				ipa->mem_offset + mem->offset;
 			req.hw_stats_quota_size_valid = 1;
-			req.hw_stats_quota_size = ipa->mem_offset + mem->size;
+			req.hw_stats_quota_size = mem->size;
 		}
 
 		/* If the DROP stats region is defined, include it */
@@ -390,7 +390,7 @@
 			req.hw_stats_drop_base_addr =
 				ipa->mem_offset + mem->offset;
 			req.hw_stats_drop_size_valid = 1;
-			req.hw_stats_drop_size = ipa->mem_offset + mem->size;
+			req.hw_stats_drop_size = mem->size;
 		}
 	}
 
